### Page 7 of 10

```text
Expedited Preliminary Plat/UDC-15-00411
5
STUDIES - The impacts identified in specific studies or technical reports that were prepared or requested
to be prepared in association with the application, and whether the findings and recommendations of
these reports, or any modifications or conditions on approval of the application, can mitigate these
impacts.

A drainage worksheet and transportation worksheet were submitted with the application. After a
review, the worksheets were found to be satisfactory by the Engineering Department.

ZONING - All proposed lots shall be buildable lots according to the existing or proposed zoning district
standards, and result in site design and development patterns that meet the Intent and Applicability
statements of the existing or proposed zoning district. All parcels not proposed as buildable lots and
which are not dedicated to and accepted by the City shall have a clearly defined entity responsible for
ongoing maintenance.

The NB District is intended for Retail, Employment, Service and Civic uses to support adjacent
residential neighborhoods in meeting most of the daily needs of residents within close proximity
to dwellings. It’s applicable in areas where small-scale retail and services are desired to support
adjacent residential uses.

The site fits into a well-connected road network, and design standards are in place to assure
transitions to adjacent sites while minimizing impacts on surrounding areas. The district
regulations are designed to encourage uses like gas stations and convenience stores, while also
protecting the abutting and nearby areas.

SURROUNDING DEVELOPMENT - The application will not create any undue influence on existing or potential
development for adjacent property considering the existing zoning and Comprehensive Plan policies for
that property.

This plat should not create any undue influence on existing or potential development within the
area.

